{
 "summary": "Found three actionable issues: duplicated channel definitions, an unused strategy extension layer, and missing behavioral tests. No functional failure appeared in fresh checks of settings validation, ordered fallback, first-success stopping, total failure, or feed reporting.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Use the canonical channel list for settings validation",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "preferences.ts:3",
   "failure": "Single Source of Truth: ALLOWED_CHANNELS duplicates CHANNELS from channels.ts:1. Channel typing derives from CHANNELS, but settings validation reads a separately maintained list. Adding a supported channel to the canonical list does not update settings acceptance, and TypeScript does not require ALLOWED_CHANNELS to contain every Channel.",
   "fix": "Import CHANNELS from channels.ts and use it directly in parseChannelOrder; delete ALLOWED_CHANNELS."
  },
  {
   "title": "Remove the strategy interface and forwarding factory",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "delivery.ts:14-19,36-38; alerts.ts:12-18",
   "failure": "Premature Abstraction: DeliveryStrategy has exactly one implementation, and createDeliveryStrategy always constructs it. AlertDispatcher is the only consumer and hard-codes that factory, so neither layer provides a selectable or injectable delivery policy. The interface and factory add contracts and indirection without adding behavior.",
   "fix": "Keep the cohesive delivery implementation, instantiate it directly in AlertDispatcher, and remove the redundant interface and factory."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add regression tests for the new alert-delivery contract",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "delivery.ts:22-32; settings-page.ts:7-8; oncall-feed.ts:4-9",
   "failure": "The patch adds no tests, and the supplied project contains no existing tests. Ordered attempts, stopping after success, failure accumulation, invalid-save atomicity, and feed reporting therefore have no persistent regression coverage. Fresh runtime assertions passed, but those checks are not part of the project.",
   "fix": "Add focused behavioral tests through saveAlertSettings and dispatchForFeed using a recording Sender. Cover first-channel success, fallback success, all-channel failure, and invalid settings leaving stored preferences unchanged."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "Fresh Bun assertions passed for normalized channel ordering; rejection of empty, duplicate, and unknown selections; unchanged preferences after rejected saves; correct addresses and message formatting; stopping at first success; ordered fallback; and feed reporting for partial and total failure."
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: Two structural issues and missing regression tests. The exercised delivery and settings behavior matched the requested intent; no behavioral intent drift was established.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Replace the fixed strategy framework with one delivery operation",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "delivery.ts:14-20,36-38; alerts.ts:12-18",
   "failure": "Premature Abstraction: DeliveryStrategy has one implementation, and createDeliveryStrategy always constructs it. AlertDispatcher fixes that choice internally, so callers cannot select or inject another policy. The interface, factory, and strategy object add coordination without providing another capability.",
   "fix": "Keep DeliveryResult and expose one delivery function, or place the fallback loop directly in AlertDispatcher. Remove the unused strategy selection layers."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add regression coverage for ordered fallback and failure reporting",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "delivery.ts:22-32; oncall-feed.ts:4-9; settings-page.ts:7-8",
   "failure": "The supplied project and patch contain no automated tests for the new behavior. Reversing the channel order, continuing after success, losing earlier failures, or storing invalid settings would have no regression check.",
   "fix": "Add tests through saveAlertSettings and dispatchForFeed with a controlled Sender. Assert ordered attempts, stopping after success, failure details including total failure, and preservation of saved settings after invalid input."
  },
  {
   "title": "Use the existing canonical channel list for validation",
   "severity": "P3",
   "location": "preferences.ts:3,20",
   "failure": "Single Source of Truth: ALLOWED_CHANNELS repeats the CHANNELS value exported by channels.ts:1. The Channel type already derives from CHANNELS, but settings validation maintains a separate list. A canonical-list update therefore also requires manual synchronization of the parser.",
   "fix": "Import CHANNELS from channels.ts and search that list instead of declaring ALLOWED_CHANNELS."
