{
 "summary": "Found two defects: Retry-After waits are truncated, and malformed numeric headers bypass backoff. All 11 existing tests pass.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "Findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Honor Retry-After instead of truncating the server's requested wait",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "retrying-transport.ts:79",
   "Failure": "Intent Drift: maxDelayMs caps server-directed waits, contradicting the requirement to honor Retry-After. A loopback HTTP probe returning 503 with Retry-After: 120 produced a 10,000 ms sleep instead of 120,000 ms under the default policy. A future HTTP date is likewise truncated. The client retries while the server still asks it to wait, potentially exhausting all attempts before recovery. Header semantics: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Retry-After .",
   "Fix": "Apply maxDelayMs only to generated exponential backoff, not valid Retry-After delays. Update the policy documentation and the existing test at retrying-transport.test.ts:67-71, which currently asserts the incorrect truncation."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Reject malformed delays before treating them as HTTP dates",
   "Severity": "P3",
   "Location": "retrying-transport.ts:77-79",
   "Failure": "The documented invalid-header fallback is incomplete because Date.parse accepts strings that are neither delay-seconds nor HTTP dates. Loopback HTTP probes with Retry-After: 1.5 and Retry-After: -1 both produced zero-delay retries rather than the default jittered backoff. Bun interprets those strings as historical dates, so the implementation skips backoff on malformed server headers. Legal forms are an HTTP date or non-negative integer seconds: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Retry-After .",
   "Fix": "Check that non-integer values have a supported HTTP-date form before parsing them; otherwise return undefined. Extend the existing invalid-header test at retrying-transport.test.ts:88-93 with decimal and signed numeric values."
  }
 ],
 "verification": [
  "bun test retrying-transport.test.ts: 11 passed, 0 failed, 19 assertions.",
  "Runtime probes covered numeric and HTTP-date Retry-After truncation.",
  "Loopback HTTP probes through FetchTransport and RetryingTransport confirmed truncation and malformed-header zero-delay retries. All probe servers were stopped."
 ]
}

